---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { REPO_URL } from "../../lib/releases";

const toc = [
  { label: "Requirements", href: "#requirements" },
  { label: "Run from source", href: "#source" },
  { label: "Package boundaries", href: "#architecture" },
  { label: "Runtime model", href: "#runtime" },
  { label: "Safe local instances", href: "#isolation" },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Local development"
  description="Run Modesto from source and understand the boundaries between the desktop app, web workspace, server, and shared contracts."
  currentPath="/docs/development"
  eyebrow="Reference"
  {toc}
>
  <section id="requirements">
    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Bun 1.3.9 or newer</li>
      <li>Node.js 24.13.1 or newer</li>
      <li>Git</li>
      <li>At least one supported coding provider for live sessions</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="source">
    <h2>Run from source</h2>
    <div class="docs-code">
      <div class="docs-code-head"><span>Quick start</span><span>Shell</span></div>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto.git
cd Modesto
bun install
bun run modesto:dev</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-table">
      <div><strong><code>bun run modesto:dev</code></strong><span>Start the Electron desktop product.</span></div>
      <div><strong><code>bun run dev:server</code></strong><span>Run the orchestration server only.</span></div>
      <div><strong><code>bun run dev:web</code></strong><span>Run the React workspace only.</span></div>
      <div><strong><code>bun run build</code></strong><span>Build the complete workspace.</span></div>
      <div><strong><code>bun run test</code></strong><span>Run the Vitest suite.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="architecture">
    <h2>Package boundaries</h2>
    <div class="docs-table">
      <div><strong><code>apps/web</code></strong><span>React workspace, session UX, timelines, diffs, terminals, and previews.</span></div>
      <div><strong><code>apps/server</code></strong><span>WebSocket RPC, provider orchestration, persistence, Git, worktrees, and terminals.</span></div>
      <div><strong><code>apps/desktop</code></strong><span>Electron lifecycle, native windows, notifications, dialogs, and updates.</span></div>
      <div><strong><code>packages/contracts</code></strong><span>Schema-only contracts shared between server and clients.</span></div>
      <div><strong><code>packages/shared</code></strong><span>Runtime utilities shared through explicit subpath exports.</span></div>
    </div>
    <p><a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/ARCHITECTURE.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the architecture reference ↗</a></p>
  </section>

  <section id="runtime">
    <h2>Runtime model</h2>
    <p>
      The current line sits on a client-server foundation: typed RPC,
      Effect services, and schema-only contracts. The server owns provider
      processes and durable orchestration. It speaks JSON-RPC to supported
      provider runtimes and projects structured domain events over WebSocket to
      the React client. The client renders the task timeline, but it is not the
      source of truth for provider state.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-table">
      <div><strong>Provider session</strong><span>A managed agent process with startup, resume, turn, interruption, and failure lifecycle.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Domain event</strong><span>A server-side record projected to clients so reconnects can rebuild predictable UI state.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Snapshot</strong><span>The current orchestration state used to hydrate projects and threads before live events continue.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="isolation">
    <h2>Run a safe local instance</h2>
    <p>
      When the desktop app is already running, use an isolated home directory
      and non-default ports. Dry-run the configuration first, then confirm the
      selected server and web ports are free before launching.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-code">
      <div class="docs-code-head"><span>Isolated development</span><span>Shell</span></div>
      <pre><code>env -u MODESTO_AUTH_TOKEN \
  MODESTO_PORT_OFFSET=3158 \
  bun run dev -- \
  --home-dir ./.modesto-docs-dev \
  --port 58090 \
  --dry-run</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
